  "narrative": {
    "essence": "Ralf Rangnick's high-intensity pressing machine returns Austria to the World Cup stage for the first time in 28 years — and they arrive not as tourists but as a team with a genuine tactical identity and the hunger to prove European football's most exciting coaching project belongs on the biggest stage.",
    "footballIdentity": "Austria punches above its weight in football as it does in culture — a small nation that produced Matthias Sindelar, one of the 1930s' most celebrated footballers, and historically fielded a 'Wunderteam' that dazzled Europe. The modern renaissance under Rangnick has reconnected Austria with that tradition of intelligent, attractive football.",
    "theMoment": "Rangnick's gegenpressing system — refined at RB Leipzig, Manchester United, and now internationally — has been built patiently into the Austrian national team since 2022. Qualifying for the 2026 World Cup after a 28-year absence is validation of the project. Dropped into a group with Argentina, Austria won't hide: they'll press, they'll run, and they'll make Group J dangerous.",
    "momentType": "footballing"
  },
